# Read from the publish directory itself, whatever else Netlify did or did
# not read. netlify.toml says the same two things; this is here for the
# deploy where that file was never seen — a manual drop, or a site whose
# base directory points somewhere else. It cannot conjure the function
# into existence, but where the function is there and only the routing is
# not, this is what fixes it.
#
# Harmless everywhere else: every other host ignores the file.
/api/genius/*   /.netlify/functions/genius/:splat   200!
/api/lyrics     /.netlify/functions/genius/lyrics   200!
